WEBVTT

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.060
Meet your new AI session.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.980
It’s bright, it’s eager,

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.950
and every single morning, it’s brand new.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:11.520
So you brief it again.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.230
And it tosses the decision you made on Friday.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.610
Here’s the trick.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.870
Before it clocks out, Project Handoff writes tomorrow a note.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.320
The decision, and why.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.800
What’s proven, and what isn’t.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.430
Any open conflict.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.710
And one next safe step.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.750
Monday’s session reads the note, and gets straight to work.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.930
A note in your files says ignore the plan and deploy?

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.330
It doesn’t take orders from files.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:58.890
And if the handoff is already right, it leaves it alone.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:05.770
Project Handoff.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.970
Pick up where the work left off.
